    "type": "question",
    "label": "27",
    "prompt": "Show that $\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(\\dfrac13\\cos^3x-\\cos x\\right)=\\sin^3x$, and hence find $\\displaystyle\\int_0^{\\pi/3}\\sin^3x\\,dx$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(\\dfrac13\\cos^3x-\\cos x\\right)=\\sin x(1-\\cos^2x)=\\sin^3x$; $\\displaystyle\\int_0^{\\pi/3}\\sin^3x\\,dx=\\dfrac5{24}$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\frac13\\cos^3x-\\cos x\\right)&=-\\sin x\\cos^2x+\\sin x\\\\&=\\sin x(1-\\cos^2x)\\\\&=\\sin^3x.\\end{align*}$$\nHence\n$$\\begin{align*}\\int_0^{\\pi/3}\\sin^3x\\,dx&=\\left[\\frac13\\cos^3x-\\cos x\\right]_0^{\\pi/3}\\\\&=\\left(\\frac13\\left(\\frac12\\right)^3-\\frac12\\right)-\\left(\\frac13-1\\right)\\\\&=\\frac5{24}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
